OHOS: recordings are staged in the app sandbox, and the system-tray
notification used by other platforms is never shown on OHOS (the tray is
intentionally disabled there), so the existing OpenRecording notification
action is unreachable. Offer the DocumentViewPicker as soon as a recording
is finalized, except for copy-only finishes, reusing the existing
RecordingFileExport path. Trim/recovery exports also offer the picker.
On OHOS, write trim-save output to the app sandbox first: the Qt file
dialog returns a document URI that QSaveFile cannot write. The sandbox
destination is chosen at publish time so it cannot collide with staging.
Keep the recording area a Qt::Tool window (capture-friendly) and focus the
recording toolbar for keyboard shortcuts. Leave trim mode and show the main
window before presenting the picker, and replace a stuck picker request.
Suppress the unsupported global-mouse startup popup on OHOS when the ACL
permission is absent, and add the OHOS input-monitor backend for HAPs signed
with the INPUT_MONITORING ACL.

